AI Log – Minnesota Corn Production Dashboard

AI Tool Used: Claude
Prompts
Build a self-contained HTML webpage for my University of St. Thomas supply chain class.

My decision question is: "How has Minnesota corn production changed over time, and how can grain suppliers use this information to plan their inventory?"

Use my downloaded USDA NASS Quick Stats CSV file containing Minnesota corn production measured in bushels.

Create a chart showing corn production by year and a dropdown that lets me select a year. Make the chart update when the selection changes.

Use real values from my CSV, not made-up data. Explain where the data comes from, where it is stored, and how it is filtered. The finished webpage must work using a saved local copy of the data, without contacting USDA.
What Went Wrong

Claude had trouble reading my original Numbers file because it was not in CSV format. It had to extract the data and convert it into a usable CSV file.

How I Checked It

I compared the data with the USDA NASS Quick Stats information and opened the dashboard in Chrome to make sure the chart and dropdown worked.

What I Learned

I learned that AI can help create a webpage, but I still need to check the data and test the webpage to make sure everything works correctly.
